:: ArgueThief
<h2 class="story-title">The Thief's Virtue</h2>

"No, NO!" the storyteller insists. "The thief overcame his very NATURE! Born to steal, raised to steal—and yet he let her pass! That's TRUE virtue!"

The necklace counters: "But the thakur overcame temptation too!"

"The thakur had wealth and status! The thief sacrificed everything—his tunnel, his plan, his profit! He went against everything he was!"

The argument grows heated...

